  "Granted $6,000 in 1914 (the state list) and dated 1915 by Vanishing Georgia; Charles Edward Choate designed it. It is still Eatonton's public library, in the Azalea regional system, and stands in the Eatonton Historic District.",
  '',
  '','309 North Madison Avenue. A working public library; its hours were not found on its own page.',
